  "text_sanskrit": "उदाराः सर्व एवैते ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम् । आस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम् ॥ ७-१८ ॥",
  "itrans": "udArAH sarva evaite j~nAnI tvAtmaiva me matam . AsthitaH sa hi yuktAtmA mAmevAnuttamA.n gatim .. 7-18 ..",
  "translation": "Great are all these without exception, but the wise man is indeed Myself (Atman only); this is My conclusion; for having devoted his mind (to Me) towards the supreme goal he has indeed come to Me. (18)\nV. In indeed Myself: is spoken of as identical with the Lord; being most beloved to Him; or being blessed with wisdom that everything depends for its existence upon the Lord. Atman only: the term Atman is also derived from the root Ap to obtain and means he who obtains, i.e., he who attains to Me. The particle Hi should be introduced after the word Eva in the first half. (18)\nA. The wise of this description are rarely met with,\"says the following”.",
